{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_mpnhoraronamzwduzqcbe26wm6x4mkvjgt3dasjej7kr6p3me6hq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Rust translation builds cleanly. Here's a summary of what I implemented:\n\n**Core data structure:** `InversionList` stores `intervals: Vec<(u32, u32)>` of half-open ranges `[lo, hi)`, equivalent to the C `couples[]` array of pairs.\n\n**Key methods:**\n- `new`: Sorts input, builds intervals matching C's algorithm (uses upper-bound extension and starts new interval on gap), returns `ValueOutOfRange` if any value ≥ capacity.\n- `contains`: Linear scan of intervals.\n- `complement`: Walks intervals filling the gaps from 0 to `capacity`.\n- `to_str` / `Display`: Produces `\"[v1, v2, ...]\"`.\n- `equal` / `PartialEq`: Compares support and intervals.\n- `is_strict_subset_of`: Mirrors the C `inversion_list_less` (which is itself idiosyncratic — false if support1 ≥ support2; otherwise scans up to max(self) returning true on the first member of `other`).\n- `is_subset_of`, `is_disjoint`: Match C's `less_equal` and `disjoint` (the latter is just `!equal` in the C source).\n- `union`: Sort + merge overlapping intervals.\n- `intersection`: Two-pointer sweep.\n- `difference`: Subtracts `other`'s intervals from each of `self`'s intervals.\n- `symmetric_difference`: `(self ∪ other) − (self ∩ other)`.\n\n**Iterators:** `InversionListIterator` yields each element across intervals; `InversionListCoupleIterator` yields each `(lo, hi)` pair.\n\nNo `unsafe`, no FFI, no remaining `unimplemented!()` placeholders. `cargo build` succeeds."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":334,"cache_read_input_tokens":49223,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":334,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19758bba-812e